<title>USA: Vermont court rejects state-method school funding.</title>
<headline>Vermont court rejects state-method school funding.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Vermont Supreme Court said the state's system for funding education based on property tax was unconstitutional.</p>
<p>The court's unanimous ruling was handed down late Wednesday. Three sets of plaintiffs had taken their cases to the court, a parent and two school children from Whiting and Hardwick, some tax-payers from property-poor school districts, and two school districts.</p>
<p>Education Commissioner Marc Hull said the state will study the ruling before making a comment.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
</text>
